-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Elite
  Publisher   Firebird, 1985
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        ELITEJCV.TAP
  MD5         7357800e60f9e230a9a700985a015725

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  The game's play area has no colour clash, so none is removed: the default
  keeps the original look. The patch adds the menu and the Next start-up. Game
  logic is unchanged (the two toggles change it, off by default).

  Changes     1.0: the standard release from its tape, original look and pace;
              IM 2 fix; 50 fps title ship; Elite.scr loading screen from
              ENTER; two gameplay toggles

  Note        The ELITEJCV (Joystick Club) tape: a frozen game with commander
              MILICEVIC; it starts at "Press Space, Commander". Original look
              and 3.5 MHz. Changes: the IM 2 interrupt works whatever the Next
              puts on the bus, and the title screens' rotating ship is redrawn
              every frame (50 fps) at the original turning speed by the game's
              own draw. Toggles, off by default, one at a time: "Bigger pirate
              packs" (3-6 a pack, not 3-4) and "Russian hack gameplay" (the
              Russian 128K hack's code and data: its ships, fonts, stars,
              fills; disk save / load off). Keys: M / N roll, S / X pitch,
              SPACE / SYMBOL SHIFT faster / slower, A laser, T / F target /
              fire missile, 1-4 views (1 launches), H hyperspace, I / O
              charts, K market, L status, P data, ENTER inventory. Known
              issues: hardware untested; the hack toggle's own logic is not
              verified.

