-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Lockstep verify against the original and the CSpect emulator;
              not yet played on a Next

  Replay      No recordings of the standard game exist: lockstep of build and
              original per instruction (PC, registers, all RAM, port writes,
              many bus bytes at the interrupt) from 24-25 scripted states per
              version (title, docked pages, launch, flight, charts,
              hyperspace, the sun, seven kinds of encounter, a missile, a long
              fight, eight equipment and end-of-game cases); every title
              render put back exactly; negative builds caught.

  Emulator    CSpect: title frames (every frame differs from the one before),
              Y / N, status page, launch and flight; both toggles boot and
              fly.

  Coverage    Scripted input, no human play: title, docked pages, launch,
              flight, charts, hyperspace, the sun, encounters, and with
              equipment set by poke the docking computer, escape pod, energy
              bomb, galactic hyperdrive, in-system jump, game over, an
              explosion and a missile hit; not reached: docking by hand, a
              full trading career.

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
